---
date added: 2026-10-26
title: Thanksgiving Turkey Meatballs and Gravy
author: Sarah DiGregorio
source: https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/792528476-thanksgiving-turkey-meatballs-and-gravy
tags: turkey, meatballs, gravy, thanksgiving, skillet, one pot, dinner
servings: 6
time required: 40 minutes
cook time: 25 minutes
---

In a large #bowl{}, whisk the @large eggs{2}. Then add the @panko bread crumbs{1%cup}, @fresh parsley{1/2%cup} (stems and leaves, finely chopped), @whole-milk Greek yogurt{1/4%cup}, @olive oil{2%tablespoons}, @garlic cloves{3} (minced), @shallots{2} (minced or ½ small onion, minced), @onion powder{2%teaspoons} (optional), @dried thyme{1 1/2%teaspoons}, @celery seeds{1 1/2%teaspoons}, @dried rosemary{1%teaspoon}, @fine kosher salt{1%tablespoon} (such as Diamond Crystal) and several generous grinds of @black pepper{}. Stir well with a fork into a thick, uniform mixture with the panko evenly moistened and the seasonings evenly distributed. Add the @ground turkey{2%pounds} (preferably 94-percent lean, or less lean, such as 80-percent lean) and mix well with your hands. Roll the mixture into 10 meatballs, each one about 2½ inches in diameter, and put them on a #plate{}.

Warm the remaining @olive oil{2%tablespoons} in a 12-inch #skillet{} over medium-high. Arrange the meatballs in the skillet (it will be snug but they should all fit) and sear, without disturbing, until the meatballs are deeply browned on one side, about ~{3%minutes}.

Flip the meatballs, adjust the heat to medium-low, and cover the pan. Cook until the meatballs are cooked through (an internal temperature of at least 160 degrees) and the second side is lightly browned, ~{12-15%minutes}. Remove the meatballs to a serving platter and cover to keep warm.

Melt the @unsalted butter{2%tablespoons} in the same skillet over medium heat. Add the @all-purpose flour{2%tablespoons} and whisk well to make a uniform paste that smells lightly toasted, about ~{1%minute}. Increase the heat to medium high, add the @chicken broth{1%cup} and whisk well to smooth the gravy, scraping up the bits on the bottom of the pan. While whisking, let the gravy come to a bubble and thicken, ~{1-2%minutes}. Squeeze in the @lemon juice{3%tablespoons} (juice of 1 large lemon) and season to taste with salt and pepper. Serve the meatballs with the gravy.
